- theta 0: {0:100, 1:100}
- theta pi/4: {0:106, 1:94}
- theta pi/2: {0:99, 1:101}
- theta 3pi/4: {0:97, 1:103}
- theta pi: {0:102, 1:98}
Every circuit gave about 50/50, whatever the angle. This is expected because the mock backend returns random results instead of simulating the circuit. A real QPU would give mostly 0 at theta 0 and mostly 1 at theta pi.
